    "TRELLIS invented a near-black back on every seed; the back is a projected rear-view concept, blended into the reconstructed texture at the sides, with the nearest painted colour carried into a few unpainted back pixels.",
    "Maps are 1024 px on the decimated TRELLIS atlas (about 57-62% coverage), whose charts touch, so filtering can show faint seams.",
    "Roughness, metalness and ambient occlusion are derived from colour inside declared regions and a Cycles bake, not measured PBR or hand-painted masks.",
    "Linear blend skinning with shoulder, hip and knee helpers: creases stretch up to about 2x at the 99.5th percentile in running and combat frames, and single edges up to about 7x at armpit, elbow and knee creases.",
    "Weapons and the quiver are low-poly Blender-authored meshes with flat painted colour, not reconstructed from a concept.",
    "Procedural clips authored in Blender (no motion capture); no root motion. Diagonal travel turns the body onto the nearest directional run (up to 45 degrees) with a counter-twisted chest instead of blending strides, and the upper body still leads the heading by up to about 35 degrees during an aimed shot or swing while running.",
    "TRELLIS textures came out far darker than the concepts, so the base colour is lifted by a luma power (toneGamma) calibrated in the game until the hero's mean brightness from the default follow camera matched the approved concept's. Sunlit front views are therefore brighter than the concept, and lifted dark saturated colours become more saturated.",
    "Re-cooking is not byte-reproducible for every hero: MikkTSpace tangents can round differently on a few vertices, and Blender's smart UV project can lay out the item atlas differently between runs.",
    "The heater shield face carries the faction dye; the body itself is not dyed, so the guard hero looks the same in every allegiance (there is only one)."
  ]
}
